<header><p class="st-kicker">theocracy · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Livonian Order</h1><p class="st-meta">1237 CE – 1561 CE · capital Wenden</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Livonian branch of the Teutonic Order, which ruled most of medieval Latvia and Estonia and fought Russia and Lithuania for three centuries.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-brothers-of-the-sword">Livonian Brothers of the Sword</a> were destroyed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-saule">Saule</a> in 1236, the survivors were incorporated into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> in 1237, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hermann-balk">Hermann Balk</a> as first master in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-confederation">Livonia</a>. The Order inherited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-brothers-of-the-sword">Sword Brothers</a>' castles and lands and their role as the military power of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/terra-mariana">Terra Mariana</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Order's knights, mostly from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a>, governed districts from stone castles under commanders and advocates, with headquarters at Riga and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesis">Wenden</a> (Cēsis). Defeats included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-on-the-ice">Lake Peipus</a> in 1242 against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-nevsky">Alexander Nevsky</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-durbe">Durbe</a> in 1260, but it conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/courland">Courland</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/semigallians">Semigallia</a> and bought <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-estonia-1219-1346">Danish Estonia</a> in 1346. It fought long wars with the archbishops of Riga and with the city itself.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Master <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolter-von-plettenberg">Wolter von Plettenberg</a> defeated <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-moscow">Muscovy</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lake-smolino">Smolina</a> in 1502, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a> from 1558 was a disaster, with defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ergeme">Ergeme</a> in 1560. In 1561 the last master, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotthard-kettler">Gotthard Kettler</a>, secularised the Order's lands, becoming Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/courland">Courland</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/semigallians">Semigallia</a> under Polish-Lithuanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/livonian-order.jpg" alt="Livonian Order" width="320" height="251"><figcaption>Image: Dirk Jansz van Santen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlas_Van_der_Hagen-KW1049B10_029-LIVONIA_Vulgo_Lyetland.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1237 CE – 1561 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>theocracy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Wenden</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hermann Balk, Wolter von Plettenberg, Gotthard Kettler</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Low German, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/latvia">Latvia</a>, <a href="/countries/estonia">Estonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Livonian Branch of the Teutonic Order, Livländischer Orden</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1399&amp;focus=livonian-order" aria-label="Livonian Order on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5217 240 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Livonian Order lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="100